This is the continuation of libsmf, a BSD-licensed C library for reading
and writing Standard MIDI Files (*.mid). It transparently handles
conversions between time and pulses, tempo maps, and more. Full API
documentation and an example program (which is also rather useful in
its own right) are also provided. libsmf was originally written and
maintained by Edward Tomasz Napierała at https://libsmf.sourceforge.net/
until 2010, then John Stumpo continued its development from 2013.
John decided to drop glib dependency on 20130723 and it was done on the
libsmf1 branch on 20130804. Later Simon Feltman started to work on the
master branch on 20131213 in order to add GObject introspection and gtk-doc
which is based on glib. Obviously the libsmf1 branch (without glib) and the
master branch (with glib) are not compatible. In this repository the libsmf1
branch is selected as base branch because glib is too much in this project.


This package has no dependencies other than the standard C library.
It builds in the usual autotools manner:

  $ ./autogen.sh  # if it's a fresh git clone
  $ ./configure [configure options]
  $ make
  # make install

Deprecated release directory:
http://ftp.stump.io/software/libsmf/

Currently there are no new releases, however there could be.
